{"timestamp":"2026-09-23T03:23:34.881Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a0cc4a-4661-7e60-af33-840705007c45","call_id":"call_7rQl9Cr3jhOeapMGXuA4e8fv","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.0 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"d87198\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000015137,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1344,\"output\":\"Entry reader leases retain segments through their final H2D completion.\\nReusable pinned routing snapshots are also returned only after completion.\\nFixed-body writers wait for earlier layer H2D before overwriting a reused slot.\\nConsumed events protect both staging contents and routing through decoder\\nlaunches. Final-reference free does not synchronize CUDA; explicit shutdown\\ndrains work before releasing the store.\\n\\nFull-block-only ownership is required. Legacy partial-block operation uses CSR\\nand reports `requires_full_block_only`. Disabling split loading or using the\\nsame stream reports serial execution. CUDA errors propagate with layer/ring\\ncontext; uncertain source completion retains the affected storage.\\n\\n## Diagnostics\\n\\nOrdinary `kv_metrics.*.csv` records raw-equivalent bytes, compressed payload,\\nactual H2D bytes, K/V bytes, routing metadata, body alignment, gaps, copy\\ndescriptors and batch calls. K includes the common output-ID metadata once.\\nHybrid additionally records `cd3_body_descriptors`, `cd3_entry_descriptors`,\\n`cd3_entry_source_spans`, and `cd3_entry_transfer`. Source spans describe the\\nselected entry ranges before compact H2D, not additional transferred bytes.\\nPayload excludes routing metadata and body padding. Raw fallback bytes are\\nincluded in aggregate KV traffic, separately from compressed CD3 counters.\\n\\nOptional CPU diagnostics separate encoding, entries packing/publication,\\nplanning and submission. Native planner counters report visited records,\\nThe load diagnostics also expose `entry_pack_cpu_ms`,\\n`transfer_wait_cpu_ms`, and `transfer_reserved_bytes` for compact transfers.\\nselected entries segments and new reusable backing allocations. Fixed result\\nobjects are not included in the backing-allocation counter. `live_payload_bytes`\\nincludes live fixed bodies and entries; `segment_capacity_bytes` describes only\\nthe entries arenas. `planner_reserved_bytes` is a conservative metadata reserve.\\n\\nThe native planner still rebuilds after membership/record invalidation. It uses\\nbounded reusable workspace and one logical plan for both rings; there is no\\nincremental segment cache or GPU segment indirection in this implementation.\\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Summarize KV traffic across workers, without importing torch or CUDA.\\n\\nThe byte sums cover recorded model forwards (including repeated KV loads).\\nServing rows are not attributable to the client's trimmed request cohort.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nimport argparse\\nimport csv\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\n\\n\\nBYTE_FIELDS = (\\\"kv_raw_bytes\\\", \\\"kv_payload_bytes\\\", \\\"kv_h2d_bytes\\\")\\nCD3_FIELDS = (\\\"cd3_k_h2d_bytes\\\", \\\"cd3_v_h2d_bytes\\\", \\\"cd3_metadata_bytes\\\",\\n              \\\"cd3_alignment_bytes\\\", \\\"cd3_gap_bytes\\\", \\\"cd3_copy_descriptors\\\", \\\"cd3_batch_calls\\\",\\n              \\\"cd3_body_descriptors\\\", \\\"cd3_entry_descriptors\\\", \\\"cd3_entry_source_spans\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef summarize(paths):\\n    groups = {}\\n    for path in paths:\\n        with open(path, newline=\\\"\\\") as source:\\n            for row in csv.DictReader(source):\\n                key = (row[\\\"config\\\"], row[\\\"batch\\\"], row[\\\"phase\\\"])\\n                if key not in groups:\\n                    groups[key] = dict(\\n                        config=key[0], batch=key[1], phase=key[2],\\n                        forwards=0, transfers=0, bytes_complete_forwards=0,\\n                        timed_forwards=0, **dict.fromkeys(BYTE_FIELDS, 0),\\n                        kvload_total_ms=0.0)\\n                    groups[key].update(dict.fromkeys(CD3_FIELDS, 0))\\n                    groups[key][\\\"cd3_accounted_forwards\\\"] = 0\\n                group = groups[key]\\n                group[\\\"forwards\\\"] += 1\\n                group[\\\"transfers\\\"] += int(row[\\\"transfers\\\"])\\n                if row[\\\"bytes_complete\\\"] == \\\"1\\\":\\n                    group[\\\"bytes_complete_forwards\\\"] += 1\\n                    for field in BYTE_FIELDS:\\n                        group[field] += int(row[field])\\n                if row[\\\"timing_complete\\\"] == \\\"1\\\":\\n                    group[\\\"timed_forwards\\\"] += 1\\n                    group[\\\"kvload_total_ms\\\"] += float(row[\\\"kvload_ms\\\"])\\n                if row.get(\\\"cd3_k_h2d_bytes\\\") not in (None, \\\"NA\\\", \\\"\\\"):\\n                    group[\\\"cd3_accounted_forwards\\\"] += 1\\n                    for field in CD3_FIELDS:\\n                        value = row.get(field)\\n                        if value in (None, \\\"NA\\\", \\\"\\\") or group[field] is None:\\n                            group[field] = None\\n                        else:\\n                            group[field] += int(value)\\n    for group in groups.values():\\n        if group[\\\"bytes_complete_forwards\\\"] != group[\\\"forwards\\\"]:\\n            for field in BYTE_FIELDS:\\n                group[field] = None\\n        raw = group[\\\"kv_raw_bytes\\\"]\\n        payload, wire = group[\\\"kv_payload_bytes\\\"], group[\\\"kv_h2d_bytes\\\"]\\n        group[\\\"kv_compression_ratio\\\"] = raw / payload if payload else None\\n        group[\\\"kv_transfer_ratio\\\"] = raw / wire if wire else None\\n        group[\\\"kv_h2d_payload_ratio\\\"] = wire / payload if payload else None\\n        if not group[\\\"cd3_accounted_forwards\\\"]:\\n            for field in CD3_FIELDS:\\n                group[field] = None\\n        if group[\\\"timed_forwards\\\"] != group[\\\"forwards\\\"]:\\n            group[\\\"kvload_total_ms\\\"] = None\\n        elapsed = group[\\\"kvload_total_ms\\\"]\\n        group[\\\"kvload_mean_ms\\\"] = (elapsed / group[\\\"forwards\\\"]\\n                                   if elapsed is not None else None)\\n    return list(groups.values())\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0cc3d-e258-7f21-a2a5-f8814ec55fb0","create_time":1790133814.8814282}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
