them. Dead or inactive entries are not transferred as gaps.\\n \\n+In `compact` mode, planning instead assigns entries offsets in body order and\\n+retains native CPU copy recipes. It skips the K/V entries sorts. Submission\\n+packs only selected Packed20x3 words into reusable pinned buffers, then sends\\n+one entries descriptor per nonempty side. Fixed bodies still transfer directly\\n+from the body pool. With nonempty K/V entries, a chunk uses `2B + 5` descriptors,\\n+where `B` is the number of body spans on one side.\\n+\\n+All layers share two K/V transfer rings. Their allocation and recipe metadata\\n+are charged against the original host allowance, reducing entries arena\\n+capacity accordingly. The CPU waits for a buffer's preceding H2D event before\\n+overwriting it. Each submission repacks its selected entries, including plan\\n+cache hits; there is no per-layer payload snapshot cache. In pipeline mode, K\\n+packing, H2D and restoration are queued before V packing begins.\\n+\\n One relative plan serves both staging rings. Native submission resolves the\\n selected ring's destination addresses. K body, entries and routing copies are\\n submitted together before the K completion event. K restoration can then run\\n@@ -80,6 +103,9 @@ context; uncertain source completion retains the affected storage.\\n Ordinary `kv_metrics.*.csv` records raw-equivalent bytes, compressed payload,\\n actual H2D bytes, K/V bytes, routing metadata, body alignment, gaps, copy\\n descriptors and batch calls. K includes the common output-ID metadata once.\\n+Hybrid additionally records `cd3_body_descriptors`, `cd3_entry_descriptors`,\\n+`cd3_entry_source_spans`, and `cd3_entry_transfer`. Source spans describe the\\n+selected entry ranges before compact H2D, not additional transferred bytes.\\n Payload excludes routing metadata and body padding. Raw fallback bytes are\\n included in aggregate KV traffic, separately from compressed CD3 counters.\\n \\n@@ -89,6 +115,8 @@ selected entri